class.description:
[MathJax] turns TeX math, such as [code]\frac{a}{b}[/code], into an SVG image with the MathJax library, which runs in a JavaScript interpreter inside the engine. No browser or network is needed, and the result is the same on every platform.
The SVG draws with [code]currentColor[/code], which becomes the text's color when replaced, and gives its size in [code]ex[/code] units, so it scales with the font it goes with. A [code]vertical-align[/code] style tells how far the formula's baseline is below its bottom.
[codeblock]
var svg := MathJax.tex_to_svg("E = mc^2")
if svg.is_empty():
    print(MathJax.get_error_message())
else:
    var texture := ImageTexture.create_from_image(Image.load_svg_from_string(svg))
[/codeblock]
MathJax loads the first time a formula is set, which takes a moment; each formula after that takes a few milliseconds.
